#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124454 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124258 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "a01560be-9023-593a-87d3-7412f3b208a3" :question/math-academy-id "e-3362" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y) = 6x^2+2y^2 - 2xy^2,$ find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y) = (3,3).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y) = k$ at the point $(x_0,y_0)$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x_0,y_0) \\cdot \\langle x-x_0, \\: y-y_0 \\rangle  = 0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y) = (3,3)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\text{ }i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2x{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(6{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2x{y}^{2})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(12x-2{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+(4y-4xy)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇\\,f(3,3) & =(12(3)-2(3)^{2})i+(4(3)-4(3)(3))j \\\\  & =18\\,i-24\\,j \\\\  & =⟨18,-24⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent to the level curve that passes through the point $(x_0,y_0)=(3,3)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(3,3)\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨18,-24⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y-3⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can leave our answer in this form. Or, if we want to leave our final answer in Cartesian form, we expand the dot product and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18(x-3)-24(y-3) & =0 \\\\ 18x-24y+18 & =0 \\\\ 3x-4y+3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/10/102f55fe0add794d3ee0f9f044b5e35c4403d4f160fe36e97d737d33ef3abb68.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050027}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521745 :question-generator/id #uuid "92fb0e69-b4c1-57e8-812c-9f971953f00f" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186124454.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3567d85d-c8e4-5c8e-a5fa-9a03f4e73154" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447336} {:answer/id #uuid "81b0821b-7e46-5c33-9092-7826606b26db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447339} {:answer/id #uuid "aad3ab95-80b7-58a9-8f7a-b59b2f76d6e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447343} {:answer/id #uuid "b3e86513-1b68-561a-a8d3-dbdeb9989260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,3⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447344} {:answer/id #uuid "dad53699-365d-5be5-97a0-c5dd9eb33c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aad3ab95-80b7-58a9-8f7a-b59b2f76d6e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447343} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbade43c-aee7-5def-a760-a6555c7e377c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ecf0fad-2e50-567b-a7b0-a4806d471317" :question/math-academy-id "q-36383" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}-y$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}-y)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}+2x{y}^{2}-y)\\,j \\\\  & =(6x+2{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+(4xy-1)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇\\,f(-1,1) & =(6(-1)+2(1)^{2})\\,i+(4(-1)(1)-1)\\,j \\\\  & =-4\\,i-5\\,j \\\\  & =⟨-4,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,1)\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-4,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b0197ad-d5e0-50ec-8157-0c06f4986576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447333} {:answer/id #uuid "341d1b1c-4578-5521-9b08-b2e4e4af8a34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447334} {:answer/id #uuid "351713ea-d6ad-5a99-b2a8-0ed43fff911d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨36,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447335} {:answer/id #uuid "e5bdc0c7-03d3-58fa-b3e6-6a56b32f6d75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,12⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447356} {:answer/id #uuid "f85e4345-3a7c-5b21-b5a8-d864dc102736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,9⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b0197ad-d5e0-50ec-8157-0c06f4986576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447333} :answer-field/id #uuid "912b4db0-e052-5337-99c9-aff6e5410f1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6369bf45-c149-5591-b6da-b79b10114d99" :question/math-academy-id "q-37517" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})-3{y}^{3}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(\\sqrt{\\pi },2).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(\\sqrt{\\pi },2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})-3{y}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})-3{y}^{3})\\,j \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2})\\,i-9{y}^{2}\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(\\sqrt{\\pi },2) & =-2\\sqrt{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡((\\sqrt{\\pi })^{2})i-9(2)^{2}\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{\\pi }\\cdot 0\\,i-36\\,j \\\\  & =-36\\,j \\\\  & =⟨0,-36⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(\\sqrt{\\pi },2)\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,-36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265823 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "053d7683-eb2b-524a-8f48-34c58516b514" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263046} {:answer/id #uuid "107f9a00-2ab2-5ddd-bcac-9802763a9723" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263152} {:answer/id #uuid "680b9d63-4091-5ae1-8e3f-46a7c9d43e8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263897} {:answer/id #uuid "dfe4251a-b496-5eb8-8465-e83d73fba9d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264944} {:answer/id #uuid "ff129e04-8125-5957-a2fe-9be8a804d26a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfe4251a-b496-5eb8-8465-e83d73fba9d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264944} :answer-field/id #uuid "afefeac9-9210-5ff6-a466-d566f40851cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "54ba14c7-96f4-538f-92f9-9aee3ad220a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130096" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1),$ find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(-1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(-1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1))\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-1,0) & =\\frac{2(-1)}{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2(0)}{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+1}\\,j \\\\  & =(-1)i+0\\,j \\\\  & =⟨-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,0)\\cdot ⟨x-(-1),\\,y-0⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fa62eab-b90e-5a48-abaf-f85a91f5acd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263290} {:answer/id #uuid "62b1fd5a-785c-5c0d-b89b-dc81b75e19f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263851} {:answer/id #uuid "a52310bc-e27c-5255-928c-7b85e9ff51e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264412} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1bcd1d-dd9d-5585-a7f9-07a54fc0555d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264626} {:answer/id #uuid "f2dab8b3-8a9a-56d3-9061-2a98e26196d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2dab8b3-8a9a-56d3-9061-2a98e26196d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265134} :answer-field/id #uuid "b246b7e5-0c53-5a83-ad21-caca0e7a4743" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265561}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7c798f0-d19a-5ddc-9430-afe4c5122532" :question/math-academy-id "q-130104" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-4xy+5{y}^{2}$ find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(-1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(-1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-4xy+5{y}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-4xy+5{y}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(2x-4y)\\,i+(10y-4x)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-1,-1) & =(2(-1)-4(-1))\\,i+(10(-1)-4(-1))\\,j \\\\  & =2\\,i-6\\,j \\\\  & =⟨2,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-(-1),\\,y-(-1)⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339099 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a942dfb1-22bb-50b2-98f2-430b4650b212" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337559} {:answer/id #uuid "cfff2df5-b768-59eb-8a42-e88ece513035" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,10⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337851} {:answer/id #uuid "d9eb05eb-aff7-5ff4-a1a3-c9872358aa4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,15⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337929} {:answer/id #uuid "f6a6cdf3-2c19-59a7-a21a-bd11e399318c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨15,10⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338196} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4820c5-0c22-53d7-866f-01894b830fd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc4820c5-0c22-53d7-866f-01894b830fd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338247} :answer-field/id #uuid "acd1dce1-2f9e-5620-9964-a61a6eed12b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36039f0f-02eb-5e5b-b0c3-c0ef4b9dcb59" :question/math-academy-id "q-72371" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+xy$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+xy)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+xy)\\,j \\\\  & =(2x{y}^{2}+y)\\,i+(2y{x}^{2}+x)\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,2) & =(2(1)(2)^{2}+(2))\\,i+(2(2)(1)^{2}+(1))\\,j \\\\  & =10\\,i+5\\,j \\\\  & =⟨10,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,2)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨10,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388076 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8440b232-2d79-53cd-bad6-36fe06f0e97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388078} {:answer/id #uuid "fec3679d-d002-508a-b44e-896ae847115f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388079} {:answer/id #uuid "d41769d3-a85e-5a1d-b0d2-621fb6f6adf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388080} {:answer/id #uuid "8d510eb4-4bca-58e9-bca7-c33fc8cc7f6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388081} {:answer/id #uuid "112648f6-f22c-57a0-8ebb-0ebd53decbdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "112648f6-f22c-57a0-8ebb-0ebd53decbdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388082} :answer-field/id #uuid "b68b09e4-9252-5d68-ab26-fe3cc2a6e217" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c1bed00-c1da-539a-bd7b-b11b7bf684ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-130094" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}-x+y,$ find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2}-x+y)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{2}-x+y)\\,j \\\\  & =({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }i+(2xy+1)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇f(1,-1) & =((-1)^{2}-1)\\,i+(2(1)(-1)+1)\\,j \\\\  & =0\\,i-j \\\\  & =⟨0,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-(-1)⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f817dec0-31ee-5a90-a6ae-2391b9cf9403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393210} {:answer/id #uuid "d27aae8e-1b41-5a3d-9baf-285744999d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393211} {:answer/id #uuid "1898f2e5-1406-5cc8-82d7-46e5635ddabe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393212} {:answer/id #uuid "4d956027-e0b5-5ae7-a8b7-35ca7afa539e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393213} {:answer/id #uuid "9b764f7f-086e-5989-aeae-04810e887220" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b764f7f-086e-5989-aeae-04810e887220" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393214} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2b7a822-706f-59e1-aaeb-ea5e1255d429" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "85c3a288-e595-578f-a534-db75ed9d872f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72377" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=2x{y}^{2}+xy+2x$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}+xy+2x)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2}+xy+2x)\\,j \\\\  & =(2{y}^{2}+y+2)\\,i+(4xy+x)\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1) & =(2(1)^{2}+(1)+2)\\,i+(4(1)(1)+(1))\\,j \\\\  & =5\\,i+5\\,j \\\\  & =⟨5,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨5,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7cd3b229-87d5-5fe0-bf43-96e6859b0b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-\\pi ⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447338} {:answer/id #uuid "8cda681d-6db9-54b3-bd78-3fc12602c207" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-\\pi ⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447340} {:answer/id #uuid "bd84b736-12f3-529d-aed6-fa8d36f93fd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-\\pi ⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447346} {:answer/id #uuid "c943eb76-7894-538d-b2d8-85356d2d0217" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-\\pi ⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447350} {:answer/id #uuid "caf722cf-879e-502b-9dcd-ed9b635a2c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-\\pi ⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd84b736-12f3-529d-aed6-fa8d36f93fd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-\\pi ⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447346} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d61b3aa-4d6d-50f6-8ee7-8efa72e96369" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c716d26-2571-5872-95a3-6c53428692e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-130102" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-y)$ find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(0,\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(0,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-y))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-y))\\,j \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}-y)\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}-y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(0,\\pi ) & =2(0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡({0}^{2}-\\pi )\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡({0}^{2}-\\pi )\\,j \\\\  & =0\\,i+j \\\\  & =⟨0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(0,\\pi )\\cdot ⟨x-0,\\,y-\\pi ⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-\\pi ⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16af8390-5001-553a-b0f4-0d97c561270f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,-10⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447330} {:answer/id #uuid "2a9a977b-a2a7-597d-813d-3e1b77c5b121" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12,14⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447332} {:answer/id #uuid "bc35064f-3e58-53ec-9341-b4fdb731d8dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447345} {:answer/id #uuid "e5a87d66-7787-5592-a30b-ee6c5d027bd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447355} {:answer/id #uuid "e6bd368a-c465-55d9-8a07-4d1ad01503a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,-11⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6bd368a-c465-55d9-8a07-4d1ad01503a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,-11⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447357} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a5737f4-7f36-5112-b8c8-5f6aec3f9ccd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7d7bf3ca-d3c4-5a27-836b-a5e78d17fbc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-36397" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=3xy+4x+6y-5{y}^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3xy+4x+6y-5{y}^{2})i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3xy+4x+6y-5{y}^{2})j \\\\  & =(3y+4)\\,i+(3x+6-10y)\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,2) & =(3(2)+4)\\,i+(3(1)+6-10(2))\\,j \\\\  & =10\\,i-11\\,j \\\\  & =⟨10,-11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,2)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨10,-11⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459277 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47412d9d-c711-5221-8676-db85828bba36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,6⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458757} {:answer/id #uuid "8e879653-b53c-5991-8c3c-66b0de773e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458876} {:answer/id #uuid "99eeb82f-f1e9-5ccc-a668-61e185f655d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,16⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458899} {:answer/id #uuid "aa41c157-f1af-54f7-be89-0b4db8719009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,18⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458934} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b40389-df84-5d28-9b01-a8cf1618fb51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,6⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e879653-b53c-5991-8c3c-66b0de773e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458876} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1c8d44b-dce1-5e85-acdf-a5ba9f5b5fab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b652bc17-f344-5009-a0c7-148f214aa2f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-36394" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y+5xy-5x{y}^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(3,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(3,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y+5xy-5x{y}^{2})i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y+5xy-5x{y}^{2})j \\\\  & =(2xy+5y-5{y}^{2})i+({x}^{2}+5x-10xy)j \\\\ ∇\\,f(3,2) & =(2(3)(2)+5(2)-5(2)^{2})i+((3)^{2}+5(3)-10(3)(2))j \\\\  & =2\\,i-36\\,j \\\\  & =⟨2,-36⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(3,2)\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2,-36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y-2⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c37ef54-3dae-58eb-86ba-e0608831b30c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,-12⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y + 2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521698} {:answer/id #uuid "61b75093-2b8c-58b7-8188-b0952cfe42de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,-12⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y + 2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521700} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0b9fd6-d82a-5b2a-959f-b39a6313e958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,-12⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y - 2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521708} {:answer/id #uuid "803e91f0-bba5-5405-ae5a-c091ede06aa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,-8⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y + 2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521713} {:answer/id #uuid "caf0597d-ab9c-5a42-82c1-3fe84a63a936" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,-12⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 1,\\,y + 2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c37ef54-3dae-58eb-86ba-e0608831b30c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,-12⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y + 2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521698} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8d79453-6692-51e6-8683-1c5f858701cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field