ten as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(- \\frac{3}{2},- \\frac{5}{2})\\cdot ⟨x-(- \\frac{3}{2}),\\,y-(- \\frac{5}{2})⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨- \\frac{111}{2},-20⟩\\cdot ⟨x + \\frac{3}{2},\\,y + \\frac{5}{2}⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bd85355-271e-50bb-88b1-d2b13a06d756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- \\frac{119}{4},\\frac{3}{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨x + \\frac{5}{2},\\,y + \\frac{1}{2}⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521693} {:answer/id #uuid "5706501c-de86-5634-87a7-ddcfe0773c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- \\frac{119}{4},\\frac{3}{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨x + \\frac{5}{2},\\,y - \\frac{1}{2}⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521697} {:answer/id #uuid "66a910cc-c44b-5f7c-b648-cb1fe9aff95d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- \\frac{119}{4},\\frac{3}{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨x - \\frac{5}{2},\\,y - \\frac{1}{2}⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521701} {:answer/id #uuid "672bcb75-b4ca-5b71-9acb-7ec472d66c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{2},- \\frac{119}{4}⟩\\cdot ⟨x + \\frac{5}{2},\\,y - \\frac{1}{2}⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521702} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3912a8-6f0e-56f9-a5f1-d09dbac9861c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{119}{4},\\frac{3}{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨x + \\frac{5}{2},\\,y - \\frac{1}{2}⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5706501c-de86-5634-87a7-ddcfe0773c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨- \\frac{119}{4},\\frac{3}{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨x + \\frac{5}{2},\\,y - \\frac{1}{2}⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521697} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e6fa0b3-7471-5b24-b6ed-74973563e2be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "973a3ce1-53a3-5558-8746-a27a1f5bd217" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=6 x^{2} + x y^{2} + 4 y^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(- \\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(- \\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6 x^{2} + x y^{2} + 4 y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(6 x^{2} + x y^{2} + 4 y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(12 x + y^{2})\\,i+(2 x y + 8 y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(- \\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{2}) & =(12 (- \\frac{5}{2}) + (\\frac{1}{2})^{2})\\,i+(2 (- \\frac{5}{2}) (\\frac{1}{2}) + 8 (\\frac{1}{2}))\\,j \\\\  & =(- \\frac{119}{4})\\,i+(\\frac{3}{2})\\,j \\\\  & =⟨- \\frac{119}{4},\\frac{3}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(- \\frac{5}{2},\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot ⟨x-(- \\frac{5}{2}),\\,y-(\\frac{1}{2})⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨- \\frac{119}{4},\\frac{3}{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨x + \\frac{5}{2},\\,y - \\frac{1}{2}⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521733 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ae7e9c8-60e9-5f5e-afbf-1de6bb01bf07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25baa447-0f3c-51cd-aaf7-6b3ac00a96e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "